              "1.Warm- up: (3’)\nMatching game\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Using pictures and flashcards, get 3 pupils hold the pictures and 3 more hold the sentences.\n- Ask them to find and match. Praise the ones who finish the matching.\n- Then ask the class to look and say aloud.\n- Say “Open your book page 52” and look at “Unit 7, Lesson 2 (1,2,3)”.\n2. Presentation(16’)\nActivity 1.  Vocabulary.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to know the vocabulary in front of starting the new lesson.\n*Procedure:\n-T elicits the new words\n+ go out                   (mime)\n+ come in             (mime)\n+ speak                      (situation)\n+ Vietnamese (explain)\n+ English   (translation)\n- T models (3 times).\n- T writes the words on the board.\n- Checking: Rub out and remember\nActivity 2.   Look, listen and repeat:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to correctly say the words and use May I ………? and Yes, you can. / No, you can’t. to ask for and give permission.\n*Procedure:\n- Have Ss look at Pictures a and b and   identify names of the speakers in the pictures.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop3/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image5.png\" alt=\"image5.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop3/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image6.png\" alt=\"image6.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Play the audio twice (sentence by sentence). Correct their pronunciation where necessary.\n- Have Ss to practice the dialogue\n- T invites a few pairs to the front of the class to practice.\n- T checks pronunciation for ss.\nActivity 3   2. Listen, point and say.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to correctly say the words and use May I ……. ? and Yes, you can. / No, you can’t. to\nask for and give permission. *Procedure:\n* Model sentences:\n- T asks Ss look at picture b and helps Ss know the structure from the dialogue.\n- T introduces new structure for Ss.\n- T explains, models and gives meaning.\n-Have Ss repeat the model sentences.\n3.Practice: (7’)\n*Drill pictures\n- Have Ss look at the pictures and identify the characters.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop3/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image7.png\" alt=\"image7.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Run through all the pictures.\n- Run through model sentences.\n- Have Ss to practise:\n+ T asks, Ss answer picture a\n+ Ss ask, T answers picture b\n+ Group A ask, group B answer picture c\n+ Group B ask, group A answer picture d\n- Ask Ss to work in pairs.\n- T controls and corrects.\n- Invite a few pairs to come to the front of the classroom and point at the pictures and say the questions and answers in front of the class.\n- T gives feedbacks.\n4.Production: (7’)\nActivity 4.    Let’s talk.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to enhance the correct use of May I …….? and Yes, you can. / No, you can’t. to ask for and give permission.\n*Procedure:\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop3/tieng_anh/tuan_12/image8.png\" alt=\"image8.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n- Have Ss look at the picture and elicit the question and the answer in context.\n+  Who are they?\n+ Where are they?\n+ What are they talking about?\n-  Put Ss work in pairs to give and respond to instructions.\n- Invite some pairs of Ss to the front of the class to act out the instructions.\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T review the vocabulary and model sentences.\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n5. Homework. (2’)\n- Learn the vocabulary and model sentences by heart\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 7, Lesson 2 (4,5,6).\nDIGITAL & AI MINI-TASK (integrated into Practice/Production – 2–3’): Show a fictional digital pupil card with one incorrect AI-style name/age sentence. Pupils compare it with the card and correct the sentence. Briefly classify “first name” as usable in class and “password/home address/phone number” as private.",
              "- Ss sing and matching \n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss open their books\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and answer\n\n\n\n\n- - Ss listen and repeat \n+ Choral repetition (3 times). \n+ Individual repetition (3 ss)\n\n\n- Ss take note\n- Ss look, remember and write\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Look at the pictures and say\n+ In picture a:  Ben asks:  May I open the book? Mr Long says:  No, you can’t.\n+ In picture b: Mai asks:  May I go out? Mr Long says: Yes, you can\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and repeat in chorus (twice)\n\n-Ss work in pairs to practice\n-Ss practice the dialogue\n\n-Ss listen\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look at the picture and answer.\n  \n-Ss listen\n-Ss listen and repeat\n\n-Ss repeat to the place\n\n\n\n\n- Ss look, listen and answer\n+ Picture a: A boy asks Mr Long for his permission to leave the classroom.\n+ Picture b:   A boy asks Mr Long for his permission to speak Vietnamese.\n+ Picture c:   A girl asks the teacher for her permission to open her book.     \n+ Picture d:  A boy asks Ms Hoa for her permission to sit down.\n\n\n-Ss listen and repeat\n\n-Ss practice in chorus\n\n\n\n-Ss work in pairs to practice\n\n-Ss point and say\n\n-Ss listen.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss look at the picture and answer\n+  A picture of a classroom in which pupils are asking the teacher for her permission to\n(open the book / close the book / stand up / sit down)\n-Ss work in pairs\n\n-Ss act out the instructions.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Ss answer the questions\n\n\n\n\n\n- Ss listen\n\n-Ss listen and clap their hands\n\n\n\n\n-Ss listen and take note\nDigital/AI pupil action: Ss compare the fictional card and sentence, correct one mismatch and state one privacy rule."
