              "1.Warm- up: (3’)\nSing: Head, shoulders, knees and toes\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Show the song on the screen.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WX8HmogNyCY\n- Ask Ss to listen, sing and dance the song.\n- Say “Open your book page 76, 77” and look at “Fun time”.\n2. Practice (30’)\nActivity 1.   Find and circle\n*Aims: Ss will be able to revise learnt vocabulary by doing the word search.\n*Procedure:\n- Have Ss look at the pictures and ask +What’s this?\n+ What can you see in the pictures?\n+ What colour is it?\n- Write the words or stick the flash cards of the words, one by one, on the board.\n- Point at each word on the board and have Ss say the word as a class.\n- Point at the picture of the school, and circle it in the word search as an example.\n- Tell Ss to find the rest of the words in the word search.\n- Have Ss check and correct their answers in pairs\n- Have Ss work in pairs, one points at the pictures and the other points at the circled words in the word search and say them aloud.\nKey:\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop3/tieng_anh/tuan_18/image3.png\" alt=\"image3.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\nActivity 2. Quiz time\n*Aims: Ss will be able to revise vocabulary and sentence patterns related to asking and answering questions that help to identify school things and their colours.\n*Procedure:\n- Elicit the words and stick the flash cards on the board one by one as Ss say the corresponding words.\n- Point at each flash card and have Ss say the word as a class.\n- Point at a flash card and elicit the answers to the questions\n+ Do you have …….?\n+What colour is it?\n+ What colour are they?\n- Hold up a textbook, point at a picture of a school thing and ask these questions again.\n- Show the class how to complete the task: Point at a picture of a school thing and ask the questions in pairs.\n- Have Ss work in pair to as and answer about their school things\n- Invite a few pairs to the front of the class to interact with each other.\nActivity 3.      Look and write\n*Aims: Ss will be able to understand how mixing two colours makes a third colour\n*Procedure:\n- T elicits the names of the three colours: red, blue, yellow.\n<img src=\"assets/khbd_images/lop3/tieng_anh/tuan_18/image4.png\" alt=\"image4.png\" style=\"max-width: 95%; height: auto;\" />\n-   Use crayons or paints to show pupils what happens when you mix red and blue.\n- Explain that this third colour is called purple. Write purple on the\nboard and model it for pupils to repeat.\n- Repeat for red and yellow (orange), yellow and blue (green).\n- Have Ss complete the colour sums.\n- Check answers together as a class.\nKey: 1. purple     2. orange   3. green\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n+ What have you learnt from the lesson today?\n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n3. Homework. (2’)\n- Prepare the first test.\nDIGITAL & AI MINI-TASK (integrated into Practice/Production – 2–3’): Show a textbook/fictional character with an AI-style caption using this/that or Mr/Ms. One caption is wrong. Pupils correct it using the lesson pattern and explain that AI can misidentify people.",
