              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame: A letter to the Santa Claus\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Divide class into 4 teams.\n- Set rules: invite 1 pupil to go to the board, look at the picture, then say aloud what toy the boy wants for Christmas. The fastest has one points for his/her team.\n(kite, car, plane, train.)\n- Encourage Ss join in the game.\n- Give point for Ss.\n- Say “Open your book page 47” and look at “Unit 17, Lesson 1 (4,5,6)”.\n\n\n2.Practice: (27’)\nActivity 1.   Listen and number:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to listen to and understand four communicative contexts in which pupils identify someone’s toys and number the correct pictures. \n*Procedure:\n-   Elicit the toys the characters are holding in the pictures.\n\n\n- T ask Ss to guess the answers.\n+ T writes Ss’guessing on the board.\n- Listen to the tape:\n+  Play the recording\n+ Play the recording again and get Ss to swap books with their partners.\n+  Play the recording again to check answers together as a class. \n+ Write the answers on the board for Ss to correct their answers. Then checks Ss’ guessing.\n-  Play the recording, sentence by sentence, for the class to listen and repeat in chorus. \nKey: 1. b   2. d   3. c   4. a\n\nActivity 2.   Look, complete and read\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and complete four target gapped dialogues with the help of the picture cues.\n*Procedure:\n- Get Ss to look at the pictures and identify the toys in the pictures.\n\n- Have Ss look at the four sentences and the pictures. Elicit and model with picture 1\n+  Ask Ss to read the sentence 1 in chorus.\n+  Ask them what is missing in the question (a car). Then have them complete the gap (He has a car).\n-Have Ss work in pairs and complete the dialogue 2, 3, 4.\n- Ask a few Ss to stand up and read the sentences aloud.\n-T gives feedbacks.\n\nKey:\n1. car 2. a kite 3. He has 4. has two\n\n Activity 3.     Let’s sing\n*Aims: Ss will be able to sing the song Their toys with the correct pronunciation and melody.\n*Procedure:\n-  Introduce the title and lyrics of the song: “Their toys”\n\n-  Play the recording for Ss to listen to the whole song.\n+ Have them repeat the title and lyrics line by line.\n+ Tell Ss to point at the pictures while singing.\n-  Play the recording all the way through for Ss to listen to pronunciation and melody of the song.\n-  Play the recording line by line for Ss to listen, repeat and point to the pictures\n-  Play the recording for Ss to sing and do actions.\n-  Ask Ss to practice singing and doing actions in pairs or groups.\n-  Invite groups to the front of the classroom to perform the song \n-T gives feedback.\n\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n  + What have you learnt from the lesson today? \n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n\n3. Homework. (3’)\n- Practice part 5 again. \n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 17, Lesson 2 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: Review detective\n- T displays 2–3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with the textbook, picture or learnt sentence pattern and correct the error.\n- Evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate AI-style answer.",
