              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame:  Who’s faster?\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings. \n*Procedure:\n- Tell Ss that they are going to look at the cards in 60 seconds, memorise the words (listening to music, singing a song, watching TV, playing football, playing volleyball, drawing a picture) then remember as many of the words as possible. \n- Put the cards on a desk or stick them on the board. Then cover them with a piece of cloth. \n- Divide the class into 2 or 4 groups. - Remove the cloth and show the cards for 60 seconds. Then cover them again. \n- In their groups, Ss try to say as many of the words as they can remember.\n- Have the groups say the names of the things aloud. \n- For each correct word, give them a star or a point.\n- The group with the most stars / points wins.\n- Say “Open your book page 57” and look at “Unit 18, Lesson 3 (4,5,6)”.\n\n2.Practice: (8’)\nActivity 1.   Read and match:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read and match the pupils with the activities that they are doing.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask Ss to attendto the icons for listening, reading and drawing and elicit the words.\n\n- Tell Ss about the activity. Give Ss time to read and match.\n- Get S to swap books with a partner. Then check the answers as a class.\n -Write the correct answers on the board for Ss to check and correct their answers.\n-  Invite Ss to read the texts aloud\n-T gives feedbacks.\nKey: 1.b      2.a      3.c\n\n3.Production: (19’)\nActivity 2.  Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be write a paragraph about what they are doing.\n*Procedure:\n- Tell the class the goal of this activity\n- Have Ss fill in the first gap together as an example. \n- Ask Ss to look at the first gap, ask What do you write here? and elicit their names (My name is….). \n- Let Ss write down the word in the gap. \n- Repeat the same procedure with the other incomplete sentences.\n- Give Ss time to write the answers in their notebooks.\n- Invite a few Ss to read aloud the paragraph they have completed in front of the class. \nKey:    Pupils’ own answers\nActivity 3.    Project.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to present their photos and tell their friends what they are doing in the photos.\n*Procedure:\n- Point at the prompt drawing and explain what they should do to complete the project.\n- Prepare two photos to share with Ss. Take a piece of paper and write the captions for the photos. Point at one photo and say: In this photo, I’m ……. and point at the other photo and say: And in this photo, I’m …….\n- Have Ss show the photos or pictures that they have prepared for the project. \n- Give the Ss time to practise their presentations by themselves. \n- Invite some Ss to present in front of the class.\n\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n  + What have you learnt from the lesson today? \n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n\n\n4. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 19- Lesson 1 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: Review detective\n- T displays 2–3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with the textbook, picture or learnt sentence pattern and correct the error.\n- Evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate AI-style answer.",
