              "1.Warm- up: (5’)\nGame:  Who’s faster?\n*Aims: to review the vocabulary and structure about greet and respond to greetings. \n*Procedure:\n- Tell Ss that they are going to look at the cards in 60 seconds, memorise the words (playing volleyball, flying a kite, skating, running, cycling, skipping) then remember as many of the words as possible. \n- Put the cards on a desk or stick them on the board. Then cover them with a piece of cloth. \n- Divide the class into 2 or 4 groups. - Remove the cloth and show the cards for 60 seconds. Then cover them again. \n- In their groups, Ss try to say as many of the words as they can remember.\n- Have the groups say the names of the things aloud. \n- For each correct word, give them a star or a point.\n- The group with the most stars / points wins.\n- Say “Open your book page 63” and look at “Unit 19, Lesson 3 (4,5,6)”.\n\n2.Practice: (8’)\nActivity 1.   Read and answer:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to read a passage and answer the questions about what someone is doing outdoors.\n*Procedure:\n- Ask Ss to attend to four questions and his / her outdoor activity in the passage.\n- Have Ss work individually.\n- Set a time limit for Ss to read and answer the questions. \n- Tell Ss to swap the answers with a partner, then check answers as a class. \n- Write the answers on the board.\n-  Invite Ss to read the texts aloud\n-T gives feedbacks.\nKey: 1. They’re in the park.  \n  2. She’s cycling. \n  3. He’s flying a kite.    \n  4. He’s playing football.\n\n3.Production: (19’)\nActivity 2.  Let’s write\n*Aims: Ss will be complete a paragraph about what a pupil and his / her friend are doing outdoors.\n*Procedure:\n- Tell the class the goal of this activity\n\n- Have Ss fill in the first gap together as an example. \n- Ask Ss to look at the first gap, ask What do they like? and elicit the words (sports and games)\n- Let Ss write down the word in the gap. \n- Repeat the same procedure with the other incomplete sentences.\n- Give Ss time to write the answers in their notebooks.\n- Invite a few Ss to read aloud the paragraph they have completed in front of the class. \nKey:    Pupils’ own answers\nActivity 3.    Project.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to trace and colour the friends, then tell the class where they are and what they are doing.\n*Procedure:\n- Have pupils work in groups.\n\n- Model by saying: Look at this boy. He is Bill. I’ll trace and colour him. Then trace and colour the character (Bill) in different colours. \n- Finally, describe the character.\n+ For example: Look! This is my friend Bill. He’s in the Central Park now. He’s skating…\n- Hand out copies of the picture to pupils and coloured pencils.\n- Give time for all groups to do their task. \n- Invite some Ss to present in front of the class tell the class about the characters they have traced and coloured, then describe where and what they are doing.\n\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n  + What have you learnt from the lesson today? \n- T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n\n\n4. Homework. (3’)\n- Prepare the new lesson: Unit 20- Lesson 1 (1,2,3).\nDigital & AI mini-task: Review detective\n- T displays 2–3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with the textbook, picture or learnt sentence pattern and correct the error.\n- Evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate AI-style answer.",
