              "1.Warm- up: (3’)\nSing: Head, shoulders, knees and toes\n*Aims: to create a friendly and active atmosphere in the class to beginning the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- Show the song on the screen.\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WX8HmogNyCY\n- Ask Ss to listen, sing and dance the song.\n- Say “Open your book page 72” and look at “Fun time”.\n\n\n2. Practice (30’)\nActivity 1.   Do the puzzle:\n*Aims: Ss will be able to revise key vocabulary and sentence patterns by doing the crossword with the picture cues and completing the gapped sentences using the words from the crossword.\n*Procedure:\n- Have Ss look at the puzzle and ask: Who do you see in the pictures? \n- Stick the flash cards of the words, one by one, on the board.\n- Point to each word on the board, and have Ss say the word as a class.\n- Point at Picture 1, elicit the word, write it in the crossword as an example. \n- Ask Ss to repeat the same procedure with the other picture cues.\n- Check the answers as a class.\nKey:\n\nActivity 2. Quiz time\n*Aims: Ss will be able to prepare the questions, interview one of their friends and write down the answers. *Procedure:\n-Tell Ss that each of them needs to interview three different classmates \n- Give Ss 10 minutes to circulate and complete their survey tables\n- After Ss have interviewed their classmates and taken notes, give them another 5 to 10 minutes to prepare to share their findings.\n- Invite different Ss to come to the front of the class and share their findings.\nActivity 3.      Look and match. Then talk.\n*Aims: Ss will be able to learn the names of baby animals and match them to their parents\n*Procedure:\n- T elicits the names of the animals:  elephant, dog, cat, tiger.\n\n-  Write puppy on the board and model it for Ss to repeat.\n- Repeat for the another animals\n- Have Ss complete the activity by drawing lines to match the baby animal to their parents.\n- Check answers together.\nKey: 1.b – dog\n2.c- cat\n3. d- tiger\n4. a- elephant.\n\n*Consolidation\n*Aims: Ss will be able consolidate and wrap up the content of the lesson.\n*Procedure:\n- T asks ss to answer the following questions:\n  + What have you learnt from the lesson today? \n+What are the core values of the lesson? (if the teacher can take from the lesson).\n - T praises some Ss who are hardworking / active/ good…. as well as encourage others to try more.\n\n3. Homework. (2’)\n- Prepare the second term test\nDigital & AI mini-task: Review detective\n- T displays 2–3 short AI-style review answers, including at least one deliberate error.\n- T asks pupils to compare each answer with the textbook, picture or learnt sentence pattern and correct the error.\n- Evidence: pupil identifies and corrects at least one inaccurate AI-style answer.",
